"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1647,"Bundar and Abu Musa narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, [saying]: Sufyan narrated to us, [saying]: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to me, from Dharr, from Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led the prayer and omitted a verse."" Ubayy ibn Ka'b was among the people, and he said: ""O Messenger of Allah, was such-and-such verse made to be forgotten, or was it abrogated?"" He said: ""It was made for me to forget it."" This is the hadith of Bundar.

Abu Musa said: from Salamah, from Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy, that the Prophet ﷺ forgot a verse from the Book of Allah, and Ubayy was among the people, so he said: ""O Messenger of Allah, was such-and-such verse made to be forgotten, or did you forget it?"" He said: ""No, rather, it was made for me to forget it."""
1648,"###
 Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Amr bin Tamim al-Misri narrated to us; they both said: Yusuf bin Adi narrated to us, who said: Marwan bin Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yahya bin Kathir al-Kahili, from Miswar bin Yazid al-Usaydi. Muhammad bin Yahya (in his narration) said: ""I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)..."" while Muhammad bin Amr said: ""The Messenger of Allah ("
